{{Quote|And I'm Leesa. Leesa Chaffni. I'm a Kessurian as you can probably tell from the pointed ears and the&hellip; What? Horns? They're not horns, although I can see why you'd think that. We call them montrals and they help us sense movement in the dark, which has proved extremely useful, as you're about to hear.|Leesa Chaffni introduces herself to [[Naldri Zuvio]]|audio=LeesaChaffni-Kessurian-JawsOfJakku.flac|<ref name="JoJ">''[[The Jaws of Jakku]]''</ref>}}
'''Kessurians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that originated in the [[Kessur system]]. They had red skin and elongated [[ear]]s and [[montral]]s, which increased their senses.

==Biology and appearance==
Kessurians were a [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]. They had typically [[Color|red]] skin, elongated and pointed [[ear]]s, and hornlike [[montral]]s above their ears. They also had rounded nubs above their eyes and below their montrals and the skin on their ears, montrals, cheeks and foreheads was mottled with lighter spots than the rest of their skin. Their [[hair]] was typically brown. Kessurians had four [[limb]]s, two arms and two legs, and five-fingered hands.<ref name="TROS VD" /> The species had at least two [[Gender|sexes]]: male<ref name="THR 1" /> and female.<ref name="TROS VD" /> Male Kessurians could grow facial hair.<ref name="THR 1" /> The Kessurians montrals allowed for increased sense of space perception<ref name="TROS VD" /> and movement, even while in the dark,<ref name="JoJ" /> and their ears were highly sensitive, allowing for keen hearing<ref name="TROS VD" /> above that of many over species.<ref name="JoJ" /> Some members of the species possessed [[Force-sensitive|Force sensitivity]].<ref name="The Orphanage">{{StoryCite|story=The Orphanage (short story)|book=Dark Legends}}</ref><ref name="THR 1" />

==Society and culture==
Originating from the [[Kessur system]],<ref name="Planetnamia" /> Kessurian society functioned as a [[monarchy]], with the second-in-line to the throne being given the title of ''[[thilas]]''.<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Kessurians in the galaxy==
Kessurian [[Jedi Master]] [[Estala Maru]] was a member of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]], stationed on the [[space station]] [[Starlight Beacon]].<ref name="THR 1" />

According to legend, a [[The Force|Force]]-sensitive Kessurian girl named [[Gee'far]] was kidnapped from an [[Gaaten orphanage|orphanage]] on [[Gaaten]] during the [[Imperial Era]] by [[the Grand Inquisitor]].<ref name="The Orphanage" />

[[Leesa Chaffni]] was a young female Kessurian who lived in [[Cratertown]] on the [[planet]] [[Jakku]] alongside her [[Parent|father]] [[Lubos]] during the [[New Republic Era]] and the following [[First Order-Resistance War]].<ref name="JoJ" />

Sometime after the reign of the [[Galactic Empire]], the ''thilas'' [[Wilsa Teshlo]], feeling trapped by the life of royalty, ran away and became a member of the [[Veiled Sorority]] [[pirate]] gang.<ref name="TROS VD" /> A Kessurian dance troupe was also present at the [[Aki-Aki]] [[Festival of the Ancestors]] on [[Pasaana]] in [[35 ABY]].<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Kessurians first appeared in the [[2019]] saga film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']].<ref name="TROS" /> They were first identified in the accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'', written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> and released alongside the film on [[December 20]], 2019.<ref name="Penguin Random House">{{Penguin|url=books/607902/star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker-the-visual-dictionary-by-pablo-hidalgo|text=Star Wars The Rise of Skywalker The Visual Dictionary}}</ref> Concept art of the species' design was created by [[Jake Lunt Davies]] for a potential [[Kijimi]] resident in the film<ref name="LuntDavies">{{Twitter|JakeLuntDavies|status/1306917645913133056|[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2020-09-18|quote=Cool. And cooler with the firepower - shame they weren't a bit more bad ass in the end. I originally drew the design to go into Kijimi so had her all in furs.|archivedate=20200918112855|nolive=1}}</ref> with the production codes "Wizard 56"<ref name="Art of TROS">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref> and "Anchorage 09c" and the nickname "Red Horn Girl".<ref name="JLD-IG">{{Instagram|url=p/CDCmt8BjS--|username=jakeluntdavies|name=[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2020-07-24|quote=According to the good old DK Visual Guide she’s a Kessurian. When I drew her she was just Anchorage 09c aka Red Horn Girl. #starwars #theriseofskywalker #conceptdesign #conceptart #conceptartist #prostheticmakeup #alien #girl #red|archivefile=File:Kessurian concept art-JakeLuntDavies.png}}</ref> [[Calum Alexander Watt]] later also created additional concept art.<ref name="Costume concept">{{Twitter|CalumAWatt|status/1306907244743847939|[[Calum Alexander Watt]]|date=2020-09-18|quote=Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker, costume concept art for Pasaana crowd, Kessurian Dance Troupe, 2018. Original creature design by Jake Lunt Davies. This one doesn't appear in the book, so thanks to @PhilSzostak for permission to share here.|archivedate=20220204214614|nolive=1}}</ref><ref name="rebel base version">{{Twitter|CalumAWatt|status/1306932597633822723|[[Calum Alexander Watt]]|date=2020-09-18|quote=Yes, I think I did a rebel base version too but she ended up as a pilot I think?|archivedate=20200918122854}}</ref> The species' look was achieved through prosthetic makeup.<ref name="Makeup-IG">{{Instagram|username=jakeluntdavies|url=p/B9z-g9ujWl2|name=[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2020-03-17|quote=Alien design by me for Rise of a Skywalker. Not sure she ever made it into the final cut. 🤷♂️. Performed by Latesha Wilson @gingin_90, prosthetic makeup by @lizbarlowmakeup in 2nd pic. Also should say sculpted by @maudiebradyart.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/UWa8p|archivefile=File:WilsonWilsa.png}}</ref>

